# Cryptocurrency Price Forecasting Competition

## Description

In this competition, students forecast the **closing price** of one cryptocurrency based on historical OHLCV data (Open, High, Low, Close, Volume). The goal is not just to match the magnitude of prices, but to align the **directional movements** of the forecast with the true closing prices.

The dataset is adapted from the G-Research Crypto Forecasting competition on Kaggle and provides time series data with equidistant timestamps. Submissions are evaluated using the **Pearson correlation coefficient** between predicted and actual closing prices.

---

## Evaluation Metric

- **Pearson Correlation Coefficient**  
  Measures the linear correlation between predicted and observed closing prices. A high score indicates your predictions **move in the same direction** as the true prices, even if the magnitude differs.

Learn more:
- [Pearson Correlation (Wikipedia)](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pearson_correlation_coefficient)
